/-
Kepler.Text.TaylorSecond.LeafGenKit — lane `wt1-emission-p2-w1` (2026-11-24).

Box-independent generality layer for the generated `w1F2` D11 leaf
chains.  Generated by `scripts/gen_kit.py` from `scripts/wtspec.py`
(the single source of truth for the op trees); no op is redefined here.

* §0a positivity combinators (`g_pos_*`): the per-box `pos` chain that
  discharges every `QInterval.inv` denominator is built from these, so
  only the six `aA/aB/aC/d4A/d4B/d4C` intervals need a `norm_num`.
* §0b generic definition layer.  `gtree_<slot>` is the op tree of one
  slot as a *function of its leaf intervals*; `gP_*`/`gE`/`gDp` are the
  matan endpoint brackets as functions of the rational endpoint.  A box
  therefore writes `def w_t_tA := gtree_tA w_t_Dlt w_t_aA` and
  `def w_t_PtA_lo := gP_direct w_t_R_tA.lo`, which is what keeps the
  per-box source in the tens of KB instead of hundreds.
* §1 `g_<slot>_mem` — 71 lemmas, one per `MAT_ORDER` slot, generic in
  the leaf intervals: the caller supplies one `QInterval` per leaf plus
  its `mem` hypothesis and the positivity of every non-constant `inv`
  denominator.  The conclusion is the *rendered* real shape, so a
  per-box consumer is `rw [sh_<slot> y4 y5 y6]; exact g_<slot>_mem …`.
* §2 `g_m_vf`/`g_mD_vf`/`g_mDD_vf` — matan value / first / second
  derivative over a whole slot interval.
* §3 `g_terminal3` — eight-way terminal glue from three interior cuts.

No `axiom` / `sorry` / `admit` / `native_decide`; audited at the tail.
-/
